examples:
Count word frequency:

words = ["a", "b", "a", "c", "b", "a"]
counts = {}
for word in words:
    counts[word] = counts.get(word, 0) + 1
print(counts)   # {'a': 3, 'b': 2, 'c': 1}

Build a lookup table with a comprehension:

names = ["Ana", "Bo", "Cid"]
name_lengths = {name: len(name) for name in names}
print(name_lengths)   # {'Ana': 3, 'Bo': 2, 'Cid': 3}

